{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791297480579,"sessionID":"ses_eee5b33e6ffeZG9tbgjq5aQyDr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"e07f9bc7-86e9-470f-85fe-85f085d7fb04","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom ledger.money import parse_amount, format_cents\nfrom ledger.parse import parse_date, parse_ledger, parse_record\nfrom ledger.report import top_items, summary_line, totals_by_item\n\n# parse_amount docstring cases\nassert parse_amount(\"0.5\") == 50\nassert parse_amount(\"$0.50\") == 50\nassert parse_amount(\"1,000\") == 100000\nassert parse_amount(\"-0.05\") == -5\nassert parse_amount(\"$1,234.56\") == 123456\nassert parse_amount(\"-$3.10\") == -310\nassert parse_amount(\"12\") == 1200\n\n# format_cents: negative example from docstring, zero, grouping\nassert format_cents(-5) == \"-$0.05\"\nassert format_cents(-100) == \"-$1.00\"\nassert format_cents(0) == \"$0.00\"\nassert format_cents(123456) == \"$1,234.56\"\n\n# parse_date\nassert parse_date(\"2026-01-02\") == (2026, 1, 2)\n\n# parse_record: lower-cased and stripped item\nrec = parse_record(\"2026-10-06 |  Widget  | 3 | $4.50\")\nassert rec == {\"date\": (2026, 10, 6), \"item\": \"widget\", \"qty\": 3, \"unit_cents\": 450}\n\n# parse_ledger: blanks and comments skipped (incl. indented comment)\nrecs = parse_ledger(\"\\n   # comment\\n2026-10-01 | A | 1 | $1.00\\n\\n2026-10-02 | B | 1 | $1.00\\n\")\nassert [r[\"item\"] for r in recs] == [\"a\", \"b\"]\n\n# top_items: descending; ties broken by name ascending\ntied = [{\"item\": \"b\", \"qty\": 1, \"unit_cents\": 100}, {\"item\": \"a\", \"qty\": 1, \"unit_cents\": 100}, {\"item\": \"c\", \"qty\": 5, \"unit_cents\": 100}]\nassert top_items(tied, 3) == [(\"c\", 500), (\"a\", 100), (\"b\", 100)]\nassert top_items(tied, 10) == [(\"c\", 500), (\"a\", 100), (\"b\", 100)]\n\n# totals_by_item sums across records; qty-0 records contribute 0\nmulti = [{\"item\": \"x\", \"qty\": 2, \"unit_cents\": 150}, {\"item\": \"x\", \"qty\": 1, \"unit_cents\": 150}]\nassert totals_by_item(multi) == {\"x\": 450}\n\n# summary_line default n=3\nrecs = parse_ledger(\"2026-10-01 | A | 1 | $1.00\\n2026-10-01 | B | 1 | $1.00\\n2026-10-01 | C | 1 | $1.00\\n2026-10-01 | D | 1 | $1.00\\n\")\nassert summary_line(recs) == \"a=$1.00; b=$1.00; c=$1.00\"\n\nprint(\"all edge cases OK\")\nEOF"},"output":"all edge cases OK\n","metadata":{"output":"all edge cases OK\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom ledger.money import parse_amount, format_cents\nfrom ledger.parse import parse_date, parse_ledger, parse_record\nfrom ledger.report import top_items, summary_line, totals_by_item\n\n# parse_amount docstring cases\nassert parse_amount(\"0.5\") == 50\nassert parse_amount(\"$0.50\") == 50\nassert parse_amount(\"1,000\") == 100000\nassert parse_amount(\"-0.05\") == -5\nassert parse_amount(\"$1,234.56\") == 123456\nassert parse_amount(\"-$3.10\") == -310\nassert parse_amount(\"12\") == 1200\n\n# format_cents: negative example from docstring, zero, grouping\nassert format_cents(-5) == \"-$0.05\"\nassert format_cents(-100) == \"-$1.00\"\nassert format_cents(0) == \"$0.00\"\nassert format_cents(123456) == \"$1,234.56\"\n\n# parse_date\nassert parse_date(\"2026-01-02\") == (2026, 1, 2)\n\n# parse_record: lower-cased and stripped item\nrec = parse_record(\"2026-10-06 |  Widget  | 3 | $4.50\")\nassert rec == {\"date\": (2026, 10, 6), \"item\": \"widget\", \"qty\": 3, \"unit_cents\": 450}\n\n# parse_ledger: blanks and comments skipped (incl. indented comment)\nrecs = parse_ledger(\"\\n   # comment\\n2026-10-01 | A | 1 | $1.00\\n\\n2026-10-02 | B | 1 | $1.00\\n\")\nassert [r[\"item\"] for r in recs] == [\"a\", \"b\"]\n\n# top_items: descending; ties broken by name ascending\ntied = [{\"item\": \"b\", \"qty\": 1, \"unit_cents\": 100}, {\"item\": \"a\", \"qty\": 1, \"unit_cents\": 100}, {\"item\": \"c\", \"qty\": 5, \"unit_cents\": 100}]\nassert top_items(tied, 3) == [(\"c\", 500), (\"a\", 100), (\"b\", 100)]\nassert top_items(tied, 10) == [(\"c\", 500), (\"a\", 100), (\"b\", 100)]\n\n# totals_by_item sums across records; qty-0 records contribute 0\nmulti = [{\"item\": \"x\", \"qty\": 2, \"unit_cents\": 150}, {\"item\": \"x\", \"qty\": 1, \"unit_cents\": 150}]\nassert totals_by_item(multi) == {\"x\": 450}\n\n# summary_line default n=3\nrecs = parse_ledger(\"2026-10-01 | A | 1 | $1.00\\n2026-10-01 | B | 1 | $1.00\\n2026-10-01 | C | 1 | $1.00\\n2026-10-01 | D | 1 | $1.00\\n\")\nassert summary_line(recs) == \"a=$1.00; b=$1.00; c=$1.00\"\n\nprint(\"all edge cases OK\")\nEOF","time":{"start":1791297480474,"end":1791297480570}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All 6 pass. Now check documented behaviour beyond visible tests, per the docstrings:\n\n1. `parse_amount`: '$1,234.56', '-$3.10', '12', '0.5'. Test: 0.5 → 50, .5 → 50, \"-0.05\" → -5, \"1,000\" → 100000, \"$0.50\" → 50.\n2. `format_cents`: negative '-$0.05' example. format_cents(-5) → \"-$0.05\". format_cents(0) → \"$0.00\". format_cents(123456) → \"$1,234.56\" (comma grouping).\n3. `parse_date`: tuple order.\n4. `parse_record`: lower-cased and stripped items — \"  Widget  \" → \"widget\".\n5. `parse_ledger`: blank lines and '#' lines skipped.\n6. `top_items`: ties broken by item name ascending. Test with two items having equal totals.\n7. `summary_line` default n=3.\n\nLet me run a quick sanity check on these edge cases.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_111a6670e0019CDLtsoLcrWINB","sessionID":"ses_eee5b33e6ffeZG9tbgjq5aQyDr","messageID":"msg_111a62783001uGxR1AYErffJc5"}}
